                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "21a22bc2-7711-3d17-94ec-8c66d5f293fa",
                        "entry_id": "f6893c5f-0dbb-3bd9-ab94-c2468dec6c84",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор., церк. покупка или продажа церковной должности или духовного сана"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ea9a5f8-bb5d-4c4f-bec1-14e7ba9b52db",
                                "sense_id": "21a22bc2-7711-3d17-94ec-8c66d5f293fa",
                                "text": "Тож делают и духовныя власти, которыя на сан Архиерейский или Иерейский, и иныя степени церковныя посвящают на мзде: и сие беззаконие нарицается святокупство и симония."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "75703e29-5acd-4320-a1c6-cc0fbf71009d",
                                "sense_id": "21a22bc2-7711-3d17-94ec-8c66d5f293fa",
                                "text": "Выказав себя человеком твердым и властным, к тому же искусным законником, новый папа заявил, что запретит симонию, приносившую кардиналам сказочные барыши."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "80247103-40fe-467b-bd9a-14b5c3315290",
                                "sense_id": "21a22bc2-7711-3d17-94ec-8c66d5f293fa",
                                "text": "В 1310—1311 годах на Переяславском соборе снова говорится о пороке симонии, который поразил всю русскую церковь снизу доверху."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "04dbc416-a0e2-434d-a79c-dc8f41a1b769",
                        "source_entry_id": "f6893c5f-0dbb-3bd9-ab94-c2468dec6c84",
                        "source_sense_id": "21a22bc2-7711-3d17-94ec-8c66d5f293fa",
                        "target_lang_word": "simony",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "simony",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "408b2737-47c9-3197-8d22-1783e1dfb583",
                                        "entry_id": "e333847b-1d89-310a-b2aa-ea0ce911c36d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The buying or selling of spiritual or sacred things, such as ecclesiastical offices, pardons, or consecrated objects."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8538005-e971-43e6-b655-576b35552134",
                                                "sense_id": "408b2737-47c9-3197-8d22-1783e1dfb583",
                                                "text": "To his eyes it had no attraction; it savoured of simony, and was likely to bring down upon him harder and more deserved strictures than any he had yet received: he positively declined to become vicar of Puddingdale under any circumstances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8cda59d8-4769-4f02-bf9c-ed128b8e7c8f",
                                                "sense_id": "408b2737-47c9-3197-8d22-1783e1dfb583",
                                                "text": "‘There are those two,’ he then said, ‘who were recently arraigned on a charge of high simony. Fancying a monstrance and stealing it and proposing to sell it. They pleaded the usual pagan ignorance.’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d24b29a6-9372-4430-bbf9-6beed5d890dc",
                                                "sense_id": "408b2737-47c9-3197-8d22-1783e1dfb583",
                                                "text": "He openly practiced simony; in other words, he sold benefices."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "942042a0-0076-4a58-86a7-ba81a4597c10",
                        "source_entry_id": "f6893c5f-0dbb-3bd9-ab94-c2468dec6c84",
                        "source_sense_id": "21a22bc2-7711-3d17-94ec-8c66d5f293fa",
                        "target_lang_word": "Simonie",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Simonie",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "192e8d09-c90f-396b-b35a-a13e3776396c",
                                        "entry_id": "0d521d1a-affe-3171-b55e-6120d0c22522",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "die Praxis (kirchliche) Ämter gegen Geld zu vergeben"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dee1084c-03c2-49a9-8ebc-e5d21bbe42a3",
                                                "sense_id": "192e8d09-c90f-396b-b35a-a13e3776396c",
                                                "text": "Damals betrieb der Staat Simonie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41c91f72-c9b5-40e8-bcc4-6d280ab34ded",
                                                "sense_id": "192e8d09-c90f-396b-b35a-a13e3776396c",
                                                "text": "„Wie gesagt waren damals Simonie (nach dem aus der Apostelgeschichte bekannten Magier Simon benannte Sünde des „geistlichen Wuchers“, Kauf und Verkauf von geistlichen Gütern und Stellen für Geld oder Geldeswert) und Nepotismus (Verwandtenbegünstigung) verbreitete Erscheinungen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3c028b5e-3cc7-4267-a9c0-89ecad28a539",
                        "source_entry_id": "f6893c5f-0dbb-3bd9-ab94-c2468dec6c84",
                        "source_sense_id": "21a22bc2-7711-3d17-94ec-8c66d5f293fa",
                        "target_lang_word": "Ämterkauf",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "275b8549-94e7-4b8f-bee4-a517eefb6c8f",
                        "source_entry_id": "f6893c5f-0dbb-3bd9-ab94-c2468dec6c84",
                        "source_sense_id": "21a22bc2-7711-3d17-94ec-8c66d5f293fa",
                        "target_lang_word": "symonia",
                        "target_lang_code": "pl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "symonia",
                                "target_lang_code": "pl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8cfdb7a-7e43-3f86-b98f-8c690276d98c",
                                        "entry_id": "232eb9db-2560-30ed-a18e-8b63f49ce3e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "praktyka sprzedawania i kupowania godności, urzędów i dóbr w czasach średniowiecza"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c1ebb50-2bbf-43a6-9b39-f5d99a0bf48a",
                                                "sense_id": "d8cfdb7a-7e43-3f86-b98f-8c690276d98c",
                                                "text": "Walka z symonią, choć nie pozbawiła całkowicie możnowładców możliwości umieszczania krewnych na wysokich kościelnych stanowiskach, zmusiła ich do poszukiwania nowych sposobów współpracy z biskupami i kanonikami."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
